  "fixes": [
    {
      "title": "Make welcome offer eligibility clear before the application is submitted.",
      "short": "Promotional terms complaints are 7.0% of Amex complaints against 2.8% at peers. Monetary relief 9.0% against 20.5%.",
      "evidence": "Promotional terms not received is 7.0% of Amex complaints against 2.8% at the other six issuers (2.5x). 40% of those Amex narratives mention a welcome or bonus offer (peers 19%) and 21% use eligibility wording (peers 8%). Amex closes 9.0% of them with monetary relief, peers 20.5%."
    },
    {
      "title": "Post rewards reliably and warn before points are lost.",
      "short": "Rewards complaints are 6.3% against 3.2% at peers. Monetary relief 11.5% against 20.6%.",
      "evidence": "Rewards problems are 6.3% of Amex complaints against 3.2% at peers (2.0x). 27% of the Amex narratives are about a welcome or bonus offer and 11% about points being forfeited or taken back. Monetary relief: Amex 11.5%, peers 20.6%. In the LLM theme labels, rewards and points is 11.0% of Amex narratives against 5.6% at peers."
    },
    {
      "title": "Set a clear annual fee refund and renewal notice policy ahead of Platinum renewals.",
      "short": "35% of Amex fee narratives are about the annual fee against 9% at peers. Monetary relief on fee complaints 24.4% against 38.7%.",
      "evidence": "35% of Amex fee narratives are about the annual fee (peers 9%) and 30% ask about a refund. Amex grants monetary relief on 24.4% of fee complaints, peers 38.7%. About 10% of all Amex narratives mention the annual fee against 2% at comparison issuers. The rate did not rise after the Platinum refresh, so this is a standing issue, and existing members only began renewing at the new fee in January 2026. In the LLM theme labels, annual fee is 4.3% of Amex narratives against 0.8% at peers."
    },
    {
      "title": "Make statement credits easy to track and fix posting-date edge cases.",
      "short": "Statement credit mentions went from 3.0% to 4.5% of Amex narratives after the refresh. An early signal.",
      "evidence": "Statement credit mentions in Amex narratives went from 3.0% in the 12 months before the Platinum refresh to 4.5% after, while comparison issuers went from 0.5% to 0.8% (difference in differences +1.1 pts, 95% interval 0.0 to 2.2). An early signal on small numbers, worth watching as the refreshed card adds more credits. In the LLM theme labels, statement credit or benefit redemption is 4.6% of Amex narratives against 0.9% at peers."
    },
    {
      "title": "Explain credit limit reductions when they happen.",
      "short": "Credit limit complaints are 2.4% against 1.4% at peers. The smallest of the five.",
      "evidence": "Credit limit decisions are 2.4% of Amex complaints against 1.4% at peers (1.7x), on 388 complaints. Smaller than the items above, so it ranks last."
